// examples/onus/partitura.exsc -- the score of "Onus Oligarchiae", Oligarchy's
// theme: a march in 5/4 in G for a small, overdressed orchestra, after
// Holst's Mars -- the col legno ostinato, the brass climbing a semitone a bar
// over a pedal -- with a jester's piccolo loose in the court and a bassoon
// that keeps trying to march in 3 + 2. Forty bars at 96 ticks a quarter,
// 480 a bar. Pure data: no `poscit`, no capability, no arithmetic. onus.exsc
// turns it into a Standard MIDI File; Oligarchy's FAUST orchestra
// (assets/onus-oligarchiae/ in that repository) plays the file.
//
// The sections, by bar: 0-3 exordium (the ostinato alone), 4-11 processio
// (the brass arrive), 12-19 scurra (the jester), 20-27 onus ascendit (the
// chromatic climb), 28-33 culmen, 34-39 coda iocosa.
//
// Every table here is printed by prototypes/onus_oracle.py --exsc from the
// oracle's own score, so the program and its oracle play the same music by
// construction; what the oracle checks independently is the encoding
// (tests/programs/onus_oligarchiae/TEST says how).
//
// Per-bar tables, forty entries. A mode is 0 rest, 1 sustain the bar, 2 the
// Mars rhythm (triplet, two quarters, two eighths, a quarter), 3 a roll of
// fifteen triplet eighths; the timpani's 1 is one stroke on the downbeat.
// A velocity of 0 is a rest whatever the mode.

// ---- ostinatum: MIDI channel 0, the col legno strings ------------------------

functio ostinati_modi() -> acies<mensura, 40> {
    redde [
        2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2,
        2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2,
        2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2,
        2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 0, 0, 1, 0
    ];
}

functio ostinati_soni() -> acies<mensura, 40> {
    redde [
        43, 43, 43, 43, 43, 43, 43, 43, 43, 43,
        43, 43, 43, 43, 43, 43, 48, 48, 50, 50,
        43, 44, 45, 46, 47, 48, 49, 50, 43, 43,
        43, 43, 43, 43, 43, 43, 0, 0, 43, 0
    ];
}

functio ostinati_vires() -> acies<mensura, 40> {
    redde [
        40, 46, 52, 58, 62, 64, 66, 68, 70, 72,
        74, 76, 50, 50, 50, 50, 52, 52, 56, 56,
        70, 74, 78, 82, 86, 90, 94, 98, 110, 112,
        114, 116, 118, 120, 120, 120, 0, 0, 112, 0
    ];
}

// ---- aes: channel 1, the brass. Three pitches a bar, 0 where silent ----------

